                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_611">York , Yorkshire. Convent of
                        Austin friars</orgName><p>This manuscript may be that given to the library
                        by John Erghome, entered at 645 in the library catalogue of 1372. The
                        Bodleian SC identifies this manuscript as a copy made from that one at York,
                        dating the script later than Erghome's time, to the first half of the
                        fifteenth century.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cf. cat.
                        645</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Liber fratris Iohannis Gillyng monachi
                     Bellalande . emptus a quodam carpentario nomine Sproxton . Anno Domini . 1477o
                     . septimo Kalendas Iunii'; 'Liber Sancte Marie de Bellalanda' (both s. xv). The
                     reference is to the Cistercian abbey of Byland (N. Yorks); Sproxton is in the
                     near vicinity.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'John Prior' (s. xvi, fol. 64v).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Donum Rich. Roberts'.</provenance>
